  "title": "Americas Utilities: Power - FERC largely rejects IRAS proposal; mixed for IPPs following CEG deals",
  "type": "sector",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-10-12",
  "insights": [
   "FERC issued an order on October 9, 2026, accepting in part and rejecting in part PJM's Interim Resource Adequacy Service (IRAS) proposal.",
   "Approved elements include the definition of 'large load' (50 MW+ peak demand) and a centralized large load registry effective October 12, 2026.",
   "Rejected elements include the IRAS curtailment construct, Bring Your Own New Capacity (BYONC) rules, and the exclusion of new large load from the Variable Resource Requirement (VRR) demand curve.",
   "The rejection of the VRR exclusion is viewed as a potential upside risk to capacity prices longer term, as PJM must now model full forecasted demand for the 2029/2030 auction.",
   "Goldman Sachs believes the decision is broadly in-line with market expectations and that recent bilateral hybrid PPA deals by CEG demonstrate that merchant generators can finalize deals without IRAS.",
   "Fundamentals for PJM-exposed IPPs remain strong with firming pricing, which could lead to positive 3Q earnings updates.",
   "Goldman Sachs maintains a positive view on IPPs, citing attractive valuations at ~8x EV/EBITDA and ~10% FCF yield on 2027 estimates (ex. CEG)."
